---
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
---

<ContentPage title="Privacy Policy | Recur">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-12">Last updated: December 2026</p>

  <div class="max-w-none space-y-10 text-foreground">
    <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      At Recur, we take your privacy seriously. This policy describes what personal information we collect and how we use it.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Site Analytics</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We use <a href="https://posthog.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">PostHog</a> to understand how people use our marketing site (<a href="https://recur.fit" class="text-primary hover:underline">recur.fit</a>). It runs in cookieless mode, which means:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies are set on your device</li>
        <li>No identifiers are stored in your browser</li>
        <li>You're not tracked across sessions or other sites</li>
        <li>Your IP address isn't stored</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
        What we measure: page views, button clicks (like the App Store badge), the country you're visiting from, and which sites send us traffic. The data is aggregated and anonymous. We honor browser Do Not Track signals.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-4">
        PostHog's privacy policy: <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" class="text-primary hover:underline">posthog.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Account Information</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">When you create a Recur account, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Workout history and preferences</li>
        <li>Information about injuries or pain points you choose to share</li>
        <li>Device information needed for the app to work</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Age Checks</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Recur is for people 13 and older. When you open the app, we ask the App Store or Google Play for your age range, where the store supports it and the law requires it. We use the answer only to decide whether you can use Recur and to turn off session recordings for anyone under 18.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        We don't store your age range on your device or our servers, we never send it to analytics, and we never use it for advertising. We check again each time you open the app.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">In the App</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We collect app usage data and crash reports so we can fix problems and make Recur better, and for adults we also record how people move through the app, with passwords hidden.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
        If you turn it on, Recur saves each finished workout's type and start and end time to Apple Health or Health Connect. We don't read any health data.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        We share information only with the providers that help us run Recur, such as hosting, analytics, crash reporting and subscription processing, and we never sell it or use it for advertising.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide, maintain, and improve Recur</li>
        <li>Personalize your workout experience</li>
        <li>Send you product updates and announcements (you can opt out anytime via the unsubscribe link in any email)</li>
        <li>Respond to your comments and questions</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        Recur is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. Where the App Store or Google Play tells us a user is under 13, the app doesn't open. If you believe a child under 13 has provided us with personal information, please contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@recur.fit" class="text-primary hover:underline">hello@recur.fit</a> and we will delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Data Security</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        We implement appropriate security measures to protect your personal information. However, no method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Your Rights</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your information</li>
        <li>Opt out of marketing communications</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Contact Us</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at
        <a href="mailto:hello@recur.fit" class="text-primary hover:underline">hello@recur.fit</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</ContentPage>
